      "message": "If the rounding stays, would you mind moving it into a helper in `mm/p3s/filemap.h`, so that `generic_fadvise()` keeps upstream\u0027s code and comments and only gets a hook after `__filemap_fdatawrite_range()`? Something like:\n\n```\n\t\tif (mm_is_p3s_4k(current-\u003emm))\n\t\t\tp3s_fadvise_widen_dontneed(inode, \u0026offset, \u0026endbyte);\n```\n\nwhere `p3s_fadvise_widen_dontneed(struct inode *inode, loff_t *offset, loff_t *endbyte)` widens the range to the 16KB pages that hold its first and last whole 4KB page (and leaves it alone if there is none), so the upstream rounding below computes the same indices as this patch.\n\nThat keeps the new locals, the 4KB/16KB comment and the rewritten rounding out of mm/fadvise.c, so upstream changes there don\u0027t conflict with it. (`mm_is_p3s_4k()` and `mm_pte_size()` already handle a NULL `mm`, so the `current-\u003emm ?` check isn\u0027t needed.)",
